# Primary seeded nucleation run (T1.4 choice), 2 GPUs.
# N = 4*30^3 = 108000 atoms at rho* = 0.95. Melt at T* = 2.0, ramp to the
# quench point T* = 0.70 over 2000 steps, hold 80000 steps. A spherical FCC
# seed of radius 4.5 (369 atoms) is frozen through the melt and for 1000
# steps after the ramp, then released; it grows through the box within
# about 60k hold steps. The unseeded liquid stays liquid at this point.
# Run: srun -n 2 --gres=gpu:2 src/pmd_cuda runs/nucleation/seeded.in
vproc       1 1 2
InitUcell   30 30 15
Density     0.95
InitTemp    2.0
DeltaT      0.005
StepAvg     500
Thermostat  1
TauT        0.1
TMelt       2.0
StepMelt    5000
TQuench     0.70
StepQuench  2000
StepHold    80000
RSeed       4.5
StepRelease 1000
XYZInterval 5000
XYZPrefix   seeded
